@startuml 002-seq-reconnect
title 002 Live Activity - Refresh / reconnect recovers state from the server

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Microsoft JhengHei"
autonumber

actor Student
participant "Student UI\n(student.js)" as SUI
actor Teacher
participant "Teacher UI\n(teacher.js)" as TUI
participant "API server\n(ws_routes)" as API
participant "Teacher guard" as AUTH
participant "ParticipationService" as PART
participant "ActivityService" as ACT
database "SQLite store\n(db.py)" as DB
participant "Visibility filter" as VIS
participant "RealtimeHub" as RT

== Student refreshes, or the socket drops ==
SUI --> Student : "Reconnecting..." (if dropped)
SUI -> SUI : retry with backoff until connected
SUI -> API : WebSocket /ws/student\n(participant cookie, if any)
API -> PART : resolve_key(token)\n-> StudentKey(activity, participant, group) or None
API -> RT : register socket with that key\n(before reading state)
note right of RT
  Registered before the state read, so a
  push made in between is not missed; the
  client applies the newest state it holds.
end note
API -> PART : student_state(key)
PART -> DB : participant by hash(token);\ncurrent (DRAFT / OPEN) activity
alt valid member of group g of the current activity
  PART -> VIS : student_view(activity, group g)
  VIS --> PART : phase, units (if OPEN),\nown group's members + submissions;\nno other-group data, no rank
  PART --> API : full student state
else member of a CLOSED activity and no current activity
  PART -> VIS : student_view(closed activity, group g)
  VIS --> PART : phase CLOSED + own group's submissions
  PART --> API : closed state (FR-025)
else no valid membership, current activity exists
  PART -> VIS : student_view(activity, membership = None)
  VIS --> PART : {id, phase, groupCount}
  PART --> API : state without membership -> join form\n(old memberships never carry over)
else no valid membership, no current activity
  PART --> API : {activity: null} -> "No activity available yet"
end
API -->> SUI : student.state
SUI --> Student : screen for the current phase\n(waiting / answering / closed),\nno re-entry of name or group

== Teacher refreshes, or the socket drops ==
TUI -> API : WebSocket /ws/teacher (teacher session cookie)
API -> AUTH : require_teacher(upgrade)
alt session missing (e.g. server restarted)
  AUTH --> API : raise TeacherRequired
  API --> TUI : close 4401
  TUI --> Teacher : passcode form (see 002-seq-teacher-unlock)
else valid session
  API -> RT : register socket (teacher set)
  API -> ACT : get_displayed_activity()\n(current DRAFT / OPEN, else latest CLOSED),\nget_dashboard(id)
  ACT -> DB : activity, units, groups + members,\nsubmissions ordered by rank
  ACT --> API : state + dashboard
  API -->> TUI : activity.state + dashboard.state
  TUI --> Teacher : current phase and full live dashboard
end

note over DB
  The database is the only source of truth
  (Constitution IV): no client state is trusted
  or needed to recover. Accepted submissions
  survive a server restart.
end note
@enduml
